        "response": {
          "bodySize": 1300,
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "size": 1300,
            "text": "{\"video\":{\"url\":\"https://v3b.fal.media/files/b/0aaf4491/-3Er5eZqEk8ONHE-LpbGm_minimax-h3.mp4\",\"content_type\":\"video/mp4\",\"file_name\":\"-3Er5eZqEk8ONHE-LpbGm_minimax-h3.mp4\",\"file_size\":253615,\"width\":480,\"height\":832,\"fps\":24.0,\"duration\":4.0,\"num_frames\":96},\"seed\":5555,\"placement\":{\"x\":0,\"y\":224,\"width\":480,\"height\":384,\"left\":0,\"top\":224,\"right\":480,\"bottom\":608},\"frame_count\":96,\"frames_per_second\":24,\"expanded_prompt\":\"integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Digital 2D graphic, Static Shot. A classic television broadcast calibration pattern is displayed across the vertical frame, with the central feed featuring bold vertical SMPTE color bars, a large white circular alignment grid, a horizontal gradient spectrum bar, and a digital white box on the right cycling numbers second-by-second. The pattern seamlessly extends above and below into continuous vertical color stripes of cyan, magenta, yellow, green, and blue, framed by subtle CRT scanline textures and dark broadcast raster borders filling the upper and lower canvas. The graphics remain steady and crisp throughout the playback.\\n\\noverall_soundscape: A steady, continuous 1kHz electronic broadcast test tone plays evenly alongside faint low-frequency electrical hum and analog CRT monitor buzz.\\n\\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A\"}"
          },
